  <h1>armillary</h1>
  <p class="lede">A minimal, operator-agnostic router. It composes whatever a workspace declares — operators, a commons, repos, and the protocols they bring — and loads each into a session at its declared time.</p>

  <p>It assumes nothing by default. A bare clone declares no modules and is still a working host, which is the point: composition is additive, and there is nothing to configure before the thing runs.</p>

  <h2>Read</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/wiki/">wiki</a> explains what the armillary is and how this studio works with AI. If you would rather run it than read about it, <a href="/start">start here</a>.</p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/studiozojer/armillary">armillary</a> — the router. <a href="https://github.com/studiozojer/armillary-core">armillary-core</a> — the composition standard and an engine that obeys it.</p>
</Base>
